&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About AlphaSense:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;The world’s most sophisticated companies rely on AlphaSense to remove uncertainty from decision-making. With market intelligence and search built on proven AI, AlphaSense delivers insights that matter from content you can trust. Our universe of public and private content includes equity research, company filings, event transcripts, expert calls, news, trade journals, and clients’ own research content.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;The acquisition of Tegus by AlphaSense in 2024 advances our shared mission to empower professionals to make smarter decisions through AI-driven market intelligence. Together, AlphaSense and Tegus will accelerate growth, innovation, and content expansion, with complementary product and content capabilities that enable users to unearth even more comprehensive insights from thousands of content sets. Our platform is trusted by over 6,000 enterprise customers, including a majority of the S&amp;amp;P 500. Founded in 2011, AlphaSense is headquartered in New York City with more than 2,000 employees across the globe and offices in the U.S., U.K., Finland, India, Singapore, Canada, and Ireland. Come join us!&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h3&gt;About the Role:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The DDQ Analyst plays an important role in supporting AlphaSense’s global sales process by helping respond to client Due Diligence Questionnaires accurately, consistently, and on time. This role sits at the intersection of Compliance, Sales, ITSecurity, Cyber, and Risk, giving the analyst strong exposure to how a global SaaS company supports enterprise customers, protects data, and manages compliance requirements.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a high-volume, process-driven role suited to someone who enjoys structure, attention to detail, and working in a fast-paced business environment. The analyst will use approved response content, documented procedures, and AI-assisted tools to move DDQs through the workflow efficiently, while also learning how to identify questions that require input from subject matter experts. It is a strong opportunity for someone who wants to build experience in compliance operations, client due diligence, information security, privacy, and risk management within a global technology company.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;What You’ll Do:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support AlphaSense’s global sales process by helping complete client Due Diligence Questionnaires accurately, consistently, and within agreed turnaround times.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Review incoming DDQs, understand the nature of the request, and process them by following established standard operating procedures, templates, and the approved internal knowledge base.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Retrieve and apply pre-approved, standardised answers to client questionnaires, ensuring each response is accurate, consistent, and aligned with approved company positions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Use AI-assisted tooling to help draft, match, and assemble questionnaire responses, while carefully reviewing all AI-generated output for accuracy before it is finalised.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify questions that fall outside the SOP or do not have an approved answer in the knowledge base, and escalate them promptly and clearly to the appropriate subject matter expert rather than improvising a response.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work cross-functionally with teams such as Compliance, Security, Privacy, Legal, Product, and Sales to help move client requests forward and support deal timelines.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Protect confidential client and company information at all times, handling sensitive security, compliance, and commercial data in line with confidentiality and data-handling policies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain accurate trackers, records, and DDQ pipeline updates to ensure requests are monitored, prioritised, and completed within defined turnaround times.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Help maintain the “Source of Truth” repository of standardised answers by flagging outdated content and adding newly approved responses under the guidance of senior team members.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage access requests for the AlphaSense Trust Library by following the documented process, enabling clients to self-serve standard security and compliance documentation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop practical experience in compliance operations, client due diligence, AI-assisted workflows, information security, privacy, and risk management within a global SaaS environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
